{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And if thus You do to me.</b> Rashi explained: Moses' strength failed like a female's — meaning he was in distress and anger and could not finish the matter and say 'You,' but said 'את' like a person sighing, who at the beginning of his sigh cannot finish his breath. And one may say: the word את — לך, בך, אתך — in both masculine and feminine forms." "<b>And let me not see my evil.</b> Let me not see any more the trouble that I am in."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Chizkuni here explicitly names Rashi (פירש״י), which is unusual for his typical compilation style but rendered faithfully as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:28.514770734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}